description:
Filed by s527b (2026-10-31, s530) from the WIDE emission-ab probe of t/op/attrs.t:451 (RT 126257 `foo(sub : bar {})`, which PCL's PPI now lexes with its Attribute -- on main the label repair DROPPED the attribute there).

perl 5.40.3 calls an anonymous sub's attribute handler ONCE, at COMPILE time (with the prototype CV); PCL's `__pcl_set_attributes` wrap calls it at RUN time, once per evaluation of the `sub` expression.

    print "0 start\n";
    sub MODIFY_CODE_ATTRIBUTES { print "attr @_[2..$#_]\n"; () }
    for (1..2) { my $s = sub : bar { 1 }; }
    print "9 end\n";

perl: `attr bar` / `0 start` / `9 end`.  main (13720073-era runpcl) and the s527b tree alike: `0 start` / `attr bar` / `attr bar` / `9 end`.  PRE-EXISTING on the ordinary attributed-anon-sub path (#3162's design: the wrap is an expression); s527b only made more spellings reach it (`(sub :ATTR {...})` at expression start, Â§7).  An unhandled attribute perl REJECTS at compile time is likewise a run-time event here.

Fix sketch: lift the handler call for a CONSTANT attribute list to load time (the eval-when of the enclosing unit), keyed by the anon sub's source position; the per-evaluation wrap then only records lvalue/method/const.  Probe the closure case first (perl passes the PROTOTYPE CV, not each closure).  Low priority: no CPAN board row is known to depend on it.  Probe file: worktree agent-a743b493df5814081 scratch/s527b/p6.pl.
